From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 13:40:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ui-egui: keep a chart's drawing primitives between frames

Every frame resolved each visible chart's series from the workbook and laid the chart out again. The result is now kept per chart and reused while its inputs are the same: the workbook (by identity, so any edit, undo, redo or recalculation on any sheet makes the chart again, and scrolling or moving the selection does not), the chart's size, the zoom, the pixel density and the fonts of the egui context. The workbook is held weakly, storing the view state with the file carries the entries over, closing a workbook drops them, and the cache is bounded (128 charts, 16 MiB, least recently used first; a chart over 4 MiB is drawn without being kept).

Tests: chart_cache unit tests (9) and tests/chart_cache.rs (6, plus an ignored measurement). Measured in the test harness, release build, 300 frames: a line chart of 4 x 2000 points 0.63 ms per frame kept against 1.03 ms made every frame; the two small charts of the sales sample show no measurable difference (0.37 ms either way). The chart picker's preview is not cached.
